:bool} object form. Step-7 fix-round-22 CRIT was precisely the HTTP 422 from sending objects instead of booleans; the regression re-opens that path. Second: MAJ-3 zero-contexts branch CAUTION message still hardcodes the wrong flag name when ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT is used. Two new MAJ block fixpoint criterion (b) on the correctness lens.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R2-CORR-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Fix-round-1 removed the generic {enabled:bool}→bool unwrap in transform() without replacing it for allow_force_pushes/allow_deletions/required_linear_history/block_creations/allow_fork_syncing. These fields are returned by GitHub's GET as {enabled:bool} objects. Sending them as objects in the PUT body causes HTTP 422, breaking real restore operations. This regresses the fix-round-22 CRIT closure (STATUS.md line 347 explicitly notes the 422 was caused by the missing unwrap).\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh line 517: else: out[key] = transform(value) — for allow_force_pushes:{enabled:false} this yields {enabled:false}, not false. RESTORE_TARGET_FORCE_PUSHES at line 916: jq -r '.allow_force_pushes // false' on the transformed payload returns the object JSON string, not 'true'/'false', silently breaking the posture-degradation check at line 930. STATUS.md line 347: fix-round-22 CRIT was 'transform did not unwrap *.enabled sub-objects for required_linear_history/allow_force_pushes/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT'. No test fixture exercises a pre-state with these fields populated.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Any real --restore invocation where the operator's captured pre-state JSON (from gh api GET) includes allow_force_pushes/{enabled:bool} will fail with HTTP 422 on the unified PUT. In break-glass scenarios this extends the outage beyond the <30-min SLO. Posture-degradation checks for force_pushes/deletions also fail silently.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Restore the {enabled:bool}→bool unwrap for the specific fields that need it (allow_force_pushes, allow_deletions, required_linear_history, block_creations, required_conversation_resolution, allow_fork_syncing, lock_branch) while EXCLUDING lock_branch from the PUT body entirely (since it has no posture-degradation flag). Alternatively: add a top-level inclusion list for the documented restore PUT fields, mapping each to its correct type. Add a test with a pre-state containing allow_force_pushes:{enabled:false}.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R2-CORR-MAJ-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"R1 MAJ-3 partial closure: the zero-contexts branch (restore_contexts==0, line 983-989) appends a CAUTION entry hardcoded to 'operator acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks' regardless of whether ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL or ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT satisfied the check. The elif branch (line 990-996) was correctly conditioned on the flag name, but the if branch was not.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh line 984: both ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL and ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT accepted. Line 989: RESTORE_CAUTION_LINES+=('- **CAUTION:** restore target removes required status checks; operator acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks.') — unconditional. When ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT=1 is used for a zero-contexts restore target, the invocation log records the wrong acknowledgement flag. The elif branch at line 996 correctly says 'acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context'.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Invocation log audit trail records incorrect acknowledgement flag for zero-contexts restore operations when the operator used --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context. A post-incident reviewer reading the log cannot determine which flag was actually used from the CAUTION line alone.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"At line 989, condition the CAUTION text on which flag was set: if [ $ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL -eq 1 ]; then emit 'acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks'; elif [ $ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT -eq 1 ]; then emit 'acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context'; fi. Add a test case that uses --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context for an empty-contexts pre-state and asserts the log CAUTION line contains 'replaces-required-check-context'.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R2-CORR-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"R1 MAJ-1 partial closure: the R1 dispatch explicitly required 'check the test added for this case' — a test verifying that a pre-state with lock_branch:{enabled:true} does not produce lock_branch:true in the PUT body. No such test exists: grep for lock_branch/required_linear_history/block_creations in the test file returns no matches.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh: zero matches for lock_branch, required_linear_history, block_creations in pre-state fixtures. enable-required-check.sh transform() line 517 else-branch verified by code inspection to yield {enabled:true} (not bool true) for lock_branch:{enabled:true}, but there is no automated regression guard.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"If a future refactor re-introduces a generic bool-coercion branch for top-level {enabled:bool} fields, no test would catch it. The absence of this test was an explicit R1 dispatch closure requirement.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a test case with a pre-state JSON containing lock_branch:{enabled:true}; assert the PUT body (put-body.json) does NOT contain lock_branch:true (boolean). Assert it contains lock_branch that is not a boolean true (either absent or as an object), and that the restore succeeds (per R2-CORR-MAJ-001's fix, it should be excluded from the PUT body entirely).\\\"}],\\\"r1_closure_summary\\\":{\\\"MAJ-1\\\":\\\"PARTIAL — generic {enabled:bool} branch removed (code verified) but no test added (→ R2-CORR-MIN-001) and the removal regresses allow_force_pushes handling (→ R2-CORR-MAJ-001)\\\",\\\"MAJ-2\\\":\\\"CLOSED — realpath + REPO_ROOT/TMP_ROOT containment at lines 299-313; allows /tmp paths per test requirements\\\",\\\"MAJ-3\\\":\\\"PARTIAL — elif (non-canonical) branch correctly conditioned; if (zero-contexts) branch still hardcodes wrong flag name (→ R2-CORR-MAJ-002)\\\",\\\"MAJ-4\\\":\\\"CLOSED — 024B-extras-2 in inline case line 207 + run_workflow_guard_case loop lines 4337-4356\\\",\\\"MAJ-5\\\":\\\"CLOSED — restore-checks-context-order-shuffled test lines 3096-3140 with pre=[a,b] after=[b,a] asserts verification passed\\\",\\\"MAJ-6/SB-003\\\":\\\"CLOSED — early rejection lines 733-736; cold-start test line 4775 asserts exit 2\\\",\\\"MAJ-7/SB-001\\\":\\\"CLOSED — ^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$ regex lines 673-676; non-release-tag test line 5019 asserts exit 2 with 'matched non-release tag'\\\",\\\"MAJ-8/SB-002\\\":\\\"CLOSED — OPERATOR set at line 316 before check_forward_mode_safety at line 814; GATE2_CAUTION_LINE at line 745 correctly expands ${OPERATOR}\\\",\\\"MAJ-9/SB-004\\\":\\\"CLOSED — validate_restore_source_json reads from stdin (line 405); single cat at line 909, piped via printf '%s' | at line 910\\\",\\\"MAJ-10\\\":\\\"CLOSED — STATUS.md lines 346+352 mark SET-EQ-001 and TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 closed 2026-05-13 with D-048\\\",\\\"MAJ-11/CG-MAJ-003\\\":\\\"CLOSED — ADOPT-001 line 1280: 'D-047 (core restore contract), D-048 (automated Gate 3 + permanence)'\\\"}}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"ffc61dc9-e96a-4d6c-af15-d7a97937ee4c\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.5306809,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":25,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":117348,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1681823,\"output_tokens\":38919,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":117348,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":4286,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":124084,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":772,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":772},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2064,\"outputTokens\":31,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002219,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":25,\"outputTokens\":38919,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1681823,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":117348,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.5284619000000002,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"e52ad97c-5016-4315-a173-80d76a5d730c\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r2-safety_bypass.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":359136,\"duration_api_ms\":360459,\"num_turns\":14,\"result\":\"I have all the evidence needed. Now I'll produce the R2 SAFETY_BYPASS review.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"lens\\\":\\\"safety_bypass\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"All 4 R1 MAJ findings closed or substantially closed; 2 carry residual MIN surfaces. SB-001 (tag-name regex): CLOSED — `^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$` present and anchored at line 673; vN.M.K-alpha, vN.M.K-rc.1, unicode lookalikes all rejected. SB-002 (OPERATOR empty): SUBSTANTIALLY CLOSED — OPERATOR set globally at line 316 before check_forward_mode_safety() at line 813; GATE2_CAUTION_LINE at line 745 correctly captures OPERATOR at call time; residual: `|| echo unknown` fallback means network failure produces `@unknown` in audit log rather than aborting (no exit 2 per R1 spec). SB-003 (no-gate-2 prior-evidence): CLOSED — lines 733–736 enforce exit 2 when ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 and prior_restore_evidence_present returns false; D-048 governance claim is now accurate; awk regex evasion analysis: sed escapes all ERE specials in target; `/` and `-` in validated repo/branch names produce correct literal matches. SB-004 (TOCTOU dual-read): CLOSED — single cat at line 909 into RESTORE_TARGET_JSON; validate_restore_source_json receives content via stdin (printf %s | python3); no downstream re-read from disk. SB-005 (wrapper-inaccessible silent accept): SUBSTANTIALLY CLOSED — warning emitted to stderr at lines 797–799; residual: log block (FORWARD_CAUTION_LINES_BLOCK) contains no record of the extraneous flag when wrapper is readable. SB-006 (symlink/realpath): CLOSED — os.path.realpath() at line 299, containment case statement at lines 307–313; symlink containment test at test line 2412 uses real `ln -s /etc/hosts`. SB-007 (wrapper grep YAML-awareness): CLOSED — heuristic comment added at lines 772–775. Three new MIN surfaces surfaced by fix-round-1 changes: SB-002 residual (unknown fallback), SB-005 residual (log block omission), and a remaining check-to-read TOCTOU window. One nit: NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI + ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION cold-start combination silently accepts the gate-bypass flag as a no-op, inconsistent with D-048.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SB-R2-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"SB-002 partial residual: OPERATOR falls back to 'unknown' on gh api user failure rather than exiting 2; R1 specified exit 2 on resolution failure.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Line 316: `OPERATOR=\\\\\\\"$(gh api user --jq '.login' 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)\\\\\\\"`. The `2>/dev/null` suppresses the error and `|| echo unknown` allows the script to proceed. On network outage, GATE2_CAUTION_LINE (line 745) records 'Operator @unknown acknowledges break-glass risk' — the bypass is logged but operator identity is lost. R1 mitigation spec said: 'exits 2 when OPERATOR resolution fails'.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator invoking the Gate 2 bypass during a network outage produces an audit log that cannot be attributed to a real identity. Forensic completeness of the CAUTION audit record is degraded; no attestation of who accepted the break-glass risk.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Replace `|| echo unknown` with `|| { echo 'error: could not resolve GitHub operator identity via gh api user; verify gh auth status' >&2; exit 2; }`. Alternatively, resolve after the CI guard and before any safety function, treating failure as a hard pre-condition rather than a fallback.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SB-R2-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"SB-005 partial residual: when --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible is passed but the wrapper IS readable, the invocation log block omits any record of the extraneous flag; only stderr receives the warning.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Lines 797–799 emit the stderr WARNING when ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE=1 and wrapper_content is non-empty. FORWARD_CAUTION_LINES_BLOCK (lines 1077–1082) appends GATE2_CAUTION_LINE and WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE; WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE is only set in the wrapper-inaccessible else branch (line 790). When wrapper is readable, WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE stays empty and the log block has no record of the flag.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Post-incident auditors reading the invocation log cannot determine that --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible was passed unnecessarily on a run where verification actually succeeded. Under a social-engineering replay scenario (an operator coached to always add the flag), there is no durable log artifact proving it was a no-op.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"When ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE=1 and wrapper is accessible, append a note to FORWARD_CAUTION_LINES_BLOCK: `- **NOTE:** --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible passed but wrapper was readable; verification was performed normally.` This closes the log-record gap without changing security posture.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SB-R2-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Check-to-read TOCTOU: realpath containment guard (line 313) is separated from the single cat read (line 909) by ~600 lines including a gh api before-state GET network call; a post-check symlink swap to a REPO_ROOT-rooted target could deliver unvalidated JSON.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"RESTORE_PRE_STATE path is realpath'd and containment-checked at lines 298–313. The file is first read at line 909 (`RESTORE_TARGET_JSON=\\\\\\\"$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\"`) after the before-state GET at lines 857–868. A symlink that already resolves inside REPO_ROOT or TMP_ROOT (passing the containment check) could be updated to point to a different file within those bounds between line 313 and line 909. The R1 dual-read TOCTOU is fixed; this remaining window is narrower but real.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Requires local filesystem write access and precise timing during the network call at line 857. Attack could substitute a different restore JSON (still within REPO_ROOT/TMP_ROOT and schema-valid) that degrades branch protection — e.g. removes enforce_admins or re-enables force-pushes. Bootstrap-only, attended context limits exploitability to insider threat or malware on operator machine.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Read the file immediately after the containment check and store in a variable; pass the in-memory content to all downstream consumers. The pattern: `RESTORE_PRE_STATE_CONTENT=\\\\\\\"$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\"; RESTORE_TARGET_JSON=\\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE_CONTENT\\\\\\\"` at line ~314 would close the window entirely. This mirrors the single-read pattern already applied to the validator pipe.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SB-R2-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI + ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION cold-start combination is silently accepted as a no-op when prior evidence is absent; D-048 states the flag 'is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check_forward_mode_safety() lines 683–707: when NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI=1 and prior evidence is absent, the function returns 0 before reaching the ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION check at lines 733–736. ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 in this path produces no GATE2_CAUTION_LINE, no sleep, and no error. D-048: 'the bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'. No mutex between NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI and ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION at arg-parse level.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Cosmetic: ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION has no effect in the cold-start path (no Gate 2 check exists there anyway). D-048 documentation constraint is technically violated. An operator coaching document that says 'always add --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification' would pass silently in cold-start context, creating confusion about which flags are active.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a mutex at arg-parse time: if NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI=1 and ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1, emit 'error: --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci is incompatible with --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification; the bypass flag requires prior --restore evidence' and exit 2. Symmetric with other mutexes at lines 280–295.\\\"}]}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"f25d807e-f5ef-4fdc-82b6-d1b720f63085\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.7500283999999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":8,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":88246,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":305443,\"output_tokens\":21696,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":88246,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":9533,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":83278,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":12476,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":12476},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1864,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002009,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":8,\"outputTokens\":21696,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":305443,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":88246,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.7480194,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"1d7fdb34-c204-486c-a65a-5ea16a3e2b9a\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
