{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"D-048|transform inclusion lists|NESTED-field leakage|TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS|lock_branch|required_linear_history|block_creations\" docs/DECISIONS.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"STATUS.md:3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-13 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface; D-048 filed)\nSTATUS.md:164:| 1 | WP-SCP-024 024B-extras split via `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` after 16 R-cycles; depth-defense surface carved to `024B-extras-2` (branch preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2`). 024B-extras-1 = current branch with surface reduced to core `--restore` + ADOPT-001 §12.8 (manual Gate 3) + CI workflow + 6 of 6 posture-degradation flags. D-048 reserved. |\nSTATUS.md:182:| 10 | R29 surfaced 1 MAJ awk false-positive on prior-restore-evidence detection (context lines from existing entries triggered exit 2); closed in fix-round-30 (commit `bde5db2`) with added-line guard in awk. R30 surfaced 2 REAL MAJ: CORR-002 covered by existing TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001; SAFE-MAJ-001 (transform exclusion-list gap allowing lock_branch/required_linear_history/block_creations through unchecked) filed as TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001. Slice at criterion (b): 0 CRIT + REAL MAJ all DEFERRED to extras-2 TFs. Merge per D-040 with documented protocol-deviation rationale. |\nSTATUS.md:191:| 4 | D-048 governance record filed (this commit) — depth-defense surface ratification: 7-component contract spanning wrapper-SHA validation with annotated-tag dereferencing, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify, transform inclusion lists, audited bypass flags (`--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` + `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible`), and mutex checks. D-048 reservation note in DECISIONS.md converted to \"consumed and filed\". |\nSTATUS.md:344:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); `run_workflow_guard_case` now exercises 024B-extras-2 tooling short-circuiting, 024D/024E/024F cohort enforcement, and 024G tooling short-circuiting. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:345:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Added strict PUT-body shape assertions to `restore-checks-canonical`, `restore-checks-wrong-context-ack`, and `restore-log-sanitization` during this fix-round. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:346:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\nSTATUS.md:347:- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\nSTATUS.md:348:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:351:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\nSTATUS.md:352:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:353:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file once, then validates and extracts `required_signatures` from the captured in-memory JSON via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:51:> **D-048 reservation note (2026-05-11):** D-048 was reserved for WP-SCP-024\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:84:| D-028 | 2026-04-28 | SCP adopts D-048 / ADR-016 Design Parity Build Method (DPBM) as a contract input for any SCP slice that produces designed visual output. Layered amendment to four-tier dispatch — prototype + flows + design principles enter the contract layer the build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \"DPBM contract\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \"applies\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, ACC, RI canary-onboarding instructions reference the DPBM contract layer. D-028 lands operationally once CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 have merged | ACCEPTED | DPBM closes a structural gap that pure-code lenses can't see — a frontend built under standard four-tier dispatch can satisfy every test and still drift from the design. Without an SCP-side adoption decision, agents working through SCP's MCP consult won't be told that the contract for visual-output work includes design artefacts. CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 (both 2026-04-28) introduce the upstream doctrine; SCP adopts at the policy layer. Full rationale + injection-mechanism specification in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:101:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` and queries workflow-runs without a branch filter; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Gate 2 automated wrapper-SHA verification is absent in extras-1; the trust-model gap is deferred to D-048 / 024B-extras-2, which will add an `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag for explicit operator acknowledgement when Gate 2 verification is skipped. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:102:| D-048 | 2026-05-13 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface as estate doctrine. Components: (1) `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` validates the supplied SHA against `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100` with annotated-tag dereferencing (per-annotated-tag `gh api git/tags/<sha>` follow-up to resolve to commit SHA), so Gate 3 SHA-pinning works regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated release tags. (2) `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag is the audited Gate 2 bypass: emits a CAUTION line to stderr, a `GATE2_CAUTION_LINE` row in the invocation-log block, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so operators can Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally; the bypass is only allowed when `prior_restore_evidence_present` returns true (Gate 3 re-enable post-break-glass), so cold-start adopters cannot accidentally bypass Gate 2. (3) `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag is required when the adopter wrapper file (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) cannot be read from the current context — without the flag, the script refuses to continue rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note. (4) `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag is the canonical-context guard: when the restore target has a non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` set that does NOT contain the canonical SCP check (`REQUIRED_CONTEXT`, default `policy-check / scp/policy-check`), restore mode requires this flag, preventing an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. (5) Set-equality verify phase replaces the prior comma-substring `grep -F` comparison with a jq `--argjson expected_contexts ... sort == sort` element-wise comparison, so legitimate restores no longer fail spuriously when GitHub returns contexts in a different order than the pre-state JSON. (6) Transform inclusion lists (`ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PULL_REQUEST_REVIEW_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS`) replace the prior exclusion-list shape in `transform()` — only documented fields pass through to the PUT body; unknown nested fields are dropped rather than leaked. (7) Mutex checks reject incompatible flag combinations (`--restore + --expected-wrapper-sha`, `--restore + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--restore + --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 is rewritten to use `--expected-wrapper-sha` automated wrapper-pin verification (replacing the manual procedure from extras-1); the Post-break-glass permanence callout is restored. `policies/VERSIONING.md` lists all 4 new posture-degradation flags as breaking-change-protected. | ACCEPTED | The depth-defense surface was operator-decided to carve out of 024B-extras after 16 R-cycles + 38 hours of session wall-time plateaued at ~5 MAJ per round, with most findings being latent depth-defects in the depth-defense surface itself (per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` + `feedback_asymptotic_trajectory_split.md`). The core `--restore` + manual-Gate-3 + workflow CI shipped in 024B-extras-1 (D-047); this slice (024B-extras-2) ratifies the depth-defense additions as separable safety properties, each adding a real defensive value: automated Gate 3 SHA-pinning eliminates operator-error on wrapper-pin verification; canonical-context guard prevents pre-state-tampering attacks; set-equality verify removes a brittle string-substring comparison; transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001); annotated-tag dereferencing makes Gate 3 work regardless of tag-format choice. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the bypass flags are explicitly auditable via stderr CAUTION + log-block CAUTION entries; the 2026-07-21 quarterly review re-evaluates single-operator posture for break-glass procedures. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras carve point (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md) + D-048 reservation. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
