{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_155","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff -- docs/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '1,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/DECISIONS.md b/docs/DECISIONS.md\nindex cc1704d..54e4845 100644\n--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -99,6 +99,6 @@\n | D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\n | D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\n | D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` and queries workflow-runs without a branch filter; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Gate 2 automated wrapper-SHA verification is absent in extras-1; the trust-model gap is deferred to D-048 / 024B-extras-2, which will add an `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag for explicit operator acknowledgement when Gate 2 verification is skipped. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\n-| D-048 | 2026-05-13 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface as estate doctrine. Components: (1) `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` validates the supplied SHA against `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100` with annotated-tag dereferencing (per-annotated-tag `gh api git/tags/<sha>` follow-up to resolve to commit SHA), so Gate 3 SHA-pinning works regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated release tags. (2) `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag is the audited Gate 2 bypass: emits a CAUTION line to stderr, a `GATE2_CAUTION_LINE` row in the invocation-log block, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so operators can Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally; the bypass is only allowed when `prior_restore_evidence_present` returns true (Gate 3 re-enable post-break-glass), so cold-start adopters cannot accidentally bypass Gate 2. (3) `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag is required when the adopter wrapper file (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) cannot be read from the current context — without the flag, the script refuses to continue rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note. (4) `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag is the canonical-context guard: when the restore target has a non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` set that does NOT contain the canonical SCP check (`REQUIRED_CONTEXT`, default `policy-check / scp/policy-check`), restore mode requires this flag, preventing an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. (5) Set-equality verify phase replaces the prior comma-substring `grep -F` comparison with a jq `--argjson expected_contexts ... sort == sort` element-wise comparison, so legitimate restores no longer fail spuriously when GitHub returns contexts in a different order than the pre-state JSON. (6) Transform inclusion lists (`ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PULL_REQUEST_REVIEW_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS`) replace the prior exclusion-list shape in `transform()` — only documented fields pass through to the PUT body; unknown nested fields are dropped rather than leaked. (7) Mutex checks reject incompatible flag combinations (`--restore + --expected-wrapper-sha`, `--restore + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--restore + --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 is rewritten to use `--expected-wrapper-sha` automated wrapper-pin verification (replacing the manual procedure from extras-1); the Post-break-glass permanence callout is restored. `policies/VERSIONING.md` lists all 4 new posture-degradation flags as breaking-change-protected. | ACCEPTED | The depth-defense surface was operator-decided to carve out of 024B-extras after 16 R-cycles + 38 hours of session wall-time plateaued at ~5 MAJ per round, with most findings being latent depth-defects in the depth-defense surface itself (per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` + `feedback_asymptotic_trajectory_split.md`). The core `--restore` + manual-Gate-3 + workflow CI shipped in 024B-extras-1 (D-047); this slice (024B-extras-2) ratifies the depth-defense additions as separable safety properties, each adding a real defensive value: automated Gate 3 SHA-pinning eliminates operator-error on wrapper-pin verification; canonical-context guard prevents pre-state-tampering attacks; set-equality verify removes a brittle string-substring comparison; transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001); annotated-tag dereferencing makes Gate 3 work regardless of tag-format choice. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the bypass flags are explicitly auditable via stderr CAUTION + log-block CAUTION entries; the 2026-07-21 quarterly review re-evaluates single-operator posture for break-glass procedures. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras carve point (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md) + D-048 reservation. |\n+| D-048 | 2026-05-13 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface as estate doctrine. Components: (1) `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` validates the supplied SHA against `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100` with annotated-tag dereferencing (per-annotated-tag `gh api git/tags/<sha>` follow-up to resolve to commit SHA), so Gate 3 SHA-pinning works regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated release tags. (2) `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag is the audited Gate 2 bypass: emits a CAUTION line to stderr, a `GATE2_CAUTION_LINE` row in the invocation-log block, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so operators can Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally; the bypass is only allowed when `prior_restore_evidence_present` returns true (Gate 3 re-enable post-break-glass), so cold-start adopters cannot accidentally bypass Gate 2. (3) `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag is required when the adopter wrapper file (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) cannot be read from the current context — without the flag, the script refuses to continue rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note. (4) `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag is the canonical-context guard: when the restore target has a non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` set that does NOT contain the canonical SCP check (`REQUIRED_CONTEXT`, default `policy-check / scp/policy-check`), restore mode requires this flag, preventing an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. (5) 